ngine/modules/grid.js)\n1512:## Module mode7: a perspective floor drawn a row at a time, a sky that turns with it, everything on it scaled by its distance (engine/modules/mode7.js)\n1535:## Module physics: 2D rigid bodies: circles, boxes, polygons, segments; fast balls that never pass through (engine/modules/physics.js)\n1564:## Module rhythm: charts on a song's steps, judged on the music clock: combos, grades, holds, a highway (engine/modules/rhythm.js)\n1596:## Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels (engine/modules/road.js)\n1613:## Module rooms: a world of rooms joined at their edges, the map of what was explored, gates and saves (engine/modules/rooms.js)\n1642:## Module rpg: items, inventories, equipment, shops, a party's stats and levels, status, damage, encounters (engine/modules/rpg.js)\n1661:## Module songs: the songbook: the kits' best songs and more, and jingles, tagged by mood (engine/modules/songs.js)\n1669:## Module story: dialogue as data, flags and values, a quest log and emote balloons (engine/modules/story.js)\n1698:## Module strategy: real-time strategy and simulation: selection, orders, armies, production, resources, placement, fog, AI; a day clock, needs, overlays (engine/modules/strategy.js)\n1744:## Module terrain: destructible ground in the side plane: carved and added, walked on, drawn in chunks (engine/modules/terrain.js)\n\n97:- 1512 Module mode7: a perspective floor drawn a row at a time, a sky that turns with it, everything on it scaled by its distance (engine/modules/mode7.js); E.Mode7: mode7\n98:- 1535 Module physics: 2D rigid bodies: circles, boxes, polygons, segments; fast balls that never pass through (engine/modules/physics.js); E.Physics: physics\n99:- 1564 Module rhythm: charts on a song's steps, judged on the music clock: combos, grades, holds, a highway (engine/modules/rhythm.js); E.Rhythm: rhythm\n100:- 1596 Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels (engine/modules/road.js); E.Road: road\n272:- `E.Input.DEFAULT { attack, dash, skill, jump }`: top-down / isometric action (Zelda, Diablo): Space dashes, J or click attacks\n276:- `E.Input.halfKeys(preset, side)` †: a preset for half a keyboard ('left' or 'right'): its moves and menu keys, the preset's other actions on its buttons in order, and the preset's gamepad codes (Input.halfKeys(Inpu\n321:- `input.use(map)`: switch key layout at runtime: input.use(E.Input.PLATFORMER) or input.use('SHMUP'). The player's own bindings (bindings, set by rebind() and the Controls screen) are laid over it. Every preset (E.I\n344:- `input.preset` †: the layout last given to use() (E.Input.DEFAULT, PLATFORMER, SHMUP or your own)\n1363:- `E.FIGHT_KEYS: up, down, left, right, lp, hp, lk, hk, start, pause, confirm, cancel` †: the fighting preset (a scene's input): the moves and menu keys of E.Input.DEFAULT, light and heavy punch (U, I; a pad's X, Y)\n1514:- `new E.Mode7(o = {}) → mode7`: new E.Mode7({ floor, size, outside, wrap, sky, fog, far }): a Mode 7 view (the manual above)\n1537:- `new E.Physics(o = {}) → physics`: new E.Physics({ gravity, substeps, iterations, sleep, on, cell }): a world of bodies (see the manual)\n1566:- `new E.Rhythm(game, o = {}) → rhythm` †: new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes, windows, life, lead, voice, on }): see the manual\n1598:- `new E.Road(o = {}) → road`: new E.Road({ segment, width, lanes, rumble, draw, fov, height, colors, fog, sky }): a road (the manual above)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6a88ba50-da75-48c3-bde0-396ebfab72e9","uuid":"1049dcd0-c6ef-471d-9b71-3d143e70c986","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:15:37.054Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1:# my-3D2dge API index (v0.89.0)\n5:## Units and the height rules\n22:## Examples\n47:## Contents\n108:## The engine object (E = My3D2dge)\n119:## 1. Math\n195:## 2. Pixel primitives\n214:## 2b. Sprite frames, tu