{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjDGn9SMSJSLx6qUgQXF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Nf2Sss6pMmAqxMjTuezipk","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ..; for m in rhythm mode7 road physics; do echo \"=== $m\"; awk '/^\\/\\*/{p=1} p{print} /\\*\\//{if(p){exit}}' modules/$m.js | cut -c1-400; done; grep -n \"shadow: '#05040a'\" my-3d2dge.js | cut -c1-200; grep -n \"r\\.ctx\\|get ctx\\|this\\.ctx =\" my-3d2dge.js | head -8 | cut -c1-160; grep -n \"^class View\\|new View(\" my-3d2dge.js | head -5 | cut -c1-200","description":"Read the rhythm, mode7, road, physics module manuals"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":23371,"cache_read_input_tokens":116190,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":23371},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6a88ba50-da75-48c3-bde0-396ebfab72e9","uuid":"c99cfb15-937d-4b3b-b2a3-cb9cf62c88b7","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:16:25.239Z","request_id":"req_011CgjDGmsa7v5JVg7GwSuhS","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Nf2Sss6pMmAqxMjTuezipk":{"command":"cd ..; for m in rhythm mode7 road physics; do echo \"=== $m\"; awk '/^\\/\\*/{p=1} p{print} /\\*\\//{if(p){exit}}' modules/$m.js | cut -c1-400; done; grep -n \"shadow: '#05040a'\" my-3d2dge.js | cut -c1-200; grep -n \"r\\.ctx\\|get ctx\\|this\\.ctx =\" my-3d2dge.js | head -8 | cut -c1-160; grep -n \"^class View\\|new View(\" my-3d2dge.js | head -5 | cut -c1-200","description":"Read the rhythm, mode7, road, physics module manuals"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Nf2Sss6pMmAqxMjTuezipk","type":"tool_result","content":"=== rhythm\n/*!\nmy-3D2dge module RHYTHM v0.89.0: charts on a song's steps, judged on the music clock: combos, grades, holds, a highway\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine only. Needs: no other module.\n\nPaRappa's, Beatmania's, Dance Dance Revolution's and Space Channel 5's play: notes on a song's steps, hit in time.\n- const rh = new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes: ['left', 'down', 'up', 'right'] (the actions, one a lane),\n  windows: { perfect: 40, great: 80, good: 120 } (ms either side), life: .5, lead: 1.6 (seconds of notes shown\n  ahead), voice: { wave: 'square', vol: .2, dur: .09 } (the call notes' sound), on: { judge(j, note), fail(rh),\n  done(rh) } }).\n- chart: a string a lane, a character a step of the song: 'x' a note, 'h' a held note's head and '=' while it is\n  held, 'c' a call (PaRappa's teacher: it sounds and shows, the player answers after), '.' none; '|' and spaces are\n  ignored. Or { parts: { A: [lanes], B: [lanes] }, order: 'A A B A' } (the parts one after another), or { track: 1,\n  lanes: 4 } (that track's notes, a lane by pitch, a note held three steps or more a hold).\n- rh.start() plays the song from its start, synced (it pauses with the game); rh.update() each step after the input:\n  a lane's press is judged by its distance in ms from its nearest note's time on the music clock (game.audio.pos:\n  game time, never the sound's own), a hold let go before its end drops, a note past the good window is missed, a\n  call sounds on its step (game.audio.sfx(voice, { step })).\n- rh.hit(lane), rh.release(lane): play a lane without its action (a bot, a lane of your own on a touch screen).\n- State: score, combo, maxCombo, counts { perfect, great, good, miss }, life (0..1, at 0 failed), accuracy (0..1),\n  grade ('S' 'A' 'B' 'C' 'D'), done, failed, last ({ j, lane, ms, t }: the last judgment, for its flash), notes\n  (each { lane, step, end, call, j, ms }), total (the notes to play).\n- rh.ahead() -> the notes to show: [{ note, dt (seconds to its time, < 0 past it), dtEnd }]; rh.draw(r, { x, y (the\n  target line's middle), dir: 'down' | 'up' | 'left' | 'right' (the way notes travel), len: 150 (pixels for lead\n  seconds), gap: 24 (between lanes), size: 8, colors, arrows: false (four lanes' notes as arrows: left, down, up,\n  right), call: false (draw the call notes instead) }) draws a highway on the overlay: the lanes, their targets, notes\n  and holds, each lane's flash.\n\n```js rhythm\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true }); game.start({ update() {}, draw() {} });\nconst song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, loop: false, len: 32, tracks: [{ wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h .' }] };\nconst rh = new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart: ['x...x...', '..x.....', '......h===', '.'] });\nrh.start(); const hits = [[0, 0], [2, 1], [4, 0], [6, 2]];\nfor (let i = 0; i < 400 && !rh.done; i++) {\n  game.advance(1 / 120); const s = game.audio.pos.step;\n  for (const h of hits) if (!h.done && s >= h[0]) { rh.hit(h[1]); h.done = true; }\n  if (s >= 9) rh.release(2); rh.update();\n}\nif (rh.counts.perfect !== 4 || rh.combo !== 4 || rh.grade !== 'S') throw new Error(JSON.stringify(rh.counts));\n```\nRules: judge on the music clock (rh does), never on the sound's; give the player the audio offset (Settings, Sound:\nits calibration) and keep the windows generous on a phone; draw notes from rh.ahead() each frame.\n*/\n=== mode7\n/*!\nmy-3D2dge module MODE7 v0.89.0: a perspective floor drawn a row at a time, a sky that turns with it, everything on it scaled by its distance\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n\nSuper Mario Kart's, F-Zero's and Pilotwings' view (the SNES's Mode 7): a camera at a height over a flat floor, looking\nalong a heading, pitched down; the floor drawn a screen row at a time, the sky above the horizon, and on the floor\nbillboards (rigs drawn at the size their distance gives, sprites, your own drawing) far to near.\n- const m7 = new E.Mode7({ floor: a TileMap (its floorTex) | (x, y) => [r, g, b] | a canvas (a texel a unit), size:\n  [w, h] (the floor in world units, for a function), outside: '#24402a' (beyond the floor) | wrap: true (it repeats),\n  sky: a Backdrop (full engine) | ['#top', '#bottom'], fog: { color, near, far } (far: nothing past it), far: 2400 }).\n- m7.cam = { x, y, h: 40 (height), angle: 0 (the heading, as E.angleTo gives it: 0 east, PI / 2 south; keep it\n  unwrapped, the sky turns with it), pitch: 12 (degrees down), fov: 70 (degrees across the height) };\n  m7.chase(body, { back: 56, h: 34, angle }) puts it behind a body (body.angle, or angle) each step.\n- In draw: m7.rig(rig, x, y, z), m7.sprite(spr or E.anim, x, y, z, { scale, flip, t }), m7.shape(id, x, y, z, { facing,\n  size, params, mats }) (full engine), m7.add(x, y, z, (g, sx, sy, k) => ...) gather billboards (k: screen pixels per world\n  unit there); m7.draw(r, cam) draws sky, floor, fog and them, far to near, as an overlay (in a split screen, in\n  r.viewport: give each player's cam). A billboard is flat, at its foot's scale: hit-test the box it was drawn in (from\n  m7.project and its size), not the world's view of it.\n- m7.project(x, y, z) -> [sx, sy, k] on the screen, or null behind the camera; m7.toFloor(sx, sy) -> [x, y], or null\n  above the horizon (both for the camera last drawn: HUD markers, a tap on the track). m7.horizon: its screen row.\n- Your own pass: m7.begin({ W, H, x, y, cx, cy, focal }, cam), then project, rowDepth(sy), drawFloor(g, rect),\n  view(k) (the engine view a rig is drawn with at k).\n- Resolution: the game's own pixels by default, as the SNES drew; m7.fullRes(game, true) each step draws at the\n  screen's own (sharper, slower; it returns the pixel size the game had), false gives the game's pixels back.\n\n```js mode7\nconst E = My3D2dge, m7 = new E.Mode7({ floor: (x, y) => ((x >> 4) + (y >> 4)) & 1 ? [80, 160, 80] : [60, 130, 60], size: [512, 512] });\nm7.cam = { x: 256, y: 400, h: 40, angle: -Math.PI / 2, pitch: 12, fov: 70 };\nm7.begin({ W: 320, H: 240 });\nconst p = m7.project(256, 300, 0), q = m7.toFloor(p[0], p[1]);\nif (Math.abs(q[0] - 256) > .01 || Math.abs(q[1] - 300) > .01 || p[1] <= m7.horizon) throw new Error('a floor point and back');\n```\nRules: m7.draw covers its viewport (draw nothing under it you need to see); move the camera in update, not draw; a\nbody's angle and the camera's heading are the same angle; billboards are gathered again every frame.\n*/\n=== road\n/*!\nmy-3D2dge module ROAD v0.89.0: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n\nOutRun's, Pole Position's, Hang-On's and Road Rash's view: the road a run of short segments, each a band of grass, rumble\nand road drawn smaller with its distance, bending and rising, and what stands beside it scaled the same way.\n- const road = new E.Road({ segment: 200 (a segment's length, world units), width: 2000 (half the road), lanes: 3,\n  rumble: 3 (segments a stripe), draw: 240 (segments ahead), fov: 100, height: 1000 (the camera over the road), colors:\n  { road: [a, b], grass: [a, b], rumble: [a, b], lane, wall: [a, b], roof, portal }, fog: { color, density: 5 } | null, sky:\n  a Backdrop (full engine) | '#color', square: true (one focal length: a unit across is a unit up on a screen of any\n  shape; without it the picture stretches to the screen's, as the arcades' did) }).\n- Build it: road.add(n, { curve: -6..6 (+ bends right), hill: units up (- down) over the n segments, tunnel: true,\n  colors }) (curves eased in and out); road.place(z, offset, what, scale): scenery at distance z, offset across (-1\n  and 1: the road's edges; beyond: roadside); what: an E.sprite or E.anim (scale: world units a pixel, 8) or {\n  draw(g, sx, sy, scale), w: its width in units }. road.length: the lap (it loops).\n- Each frame: road.draw(r, { z (the camera's distance along), x (across, in half roads), h (its height over the road),\n  turn (the sky's offset: add curve * speed each step), cars: [{ z, x, w, draw(g, sx, sy, scale) }] }) as an overlay\n  over the frame (in a split screen, in r.viewport). A hill's crest hides what lies past it. The player's car, drawn\n  at the screen's bottom, is road.ahead(h) past z.\n- For the game: road.curveAt(z) (how hard it bends there: the push outward), road.yAt(z) (its height), road.hits(z, x,\n  w) (the scenery a body w half roads wide touches there), road.project(z, x, y) -> [sx, sy, scale] for the camera\n  last drawn (scale * a width in units = pixels).\n\n```js road\nconst E = My3D2dge, road = new E.Road({ segment: 200 });\nroad.add(50); road.add(60, { curve: 4, hill: 1200 }); road.add(40, { curve: -3, hill: -1200 }); road.place(3000, -1.4, { w: 300, draw() {} });\nif (road.length !== 150 * 200 || road.curveAt(80 * 200) <= 0 || !(road.yAt(110 * 200) > 0) || road.hits(3000, -1.3, .1).length !== 1) throw new Error('a road');\n```\nRules: z grows ahead and wraps at road.length; x is in half roads (0 the middle line); build the road before the first\ndraw; cars and scenery are drawn far to near after the road under them.\n*/\n=== physics\n/*!\nmy-3D2dge module PHYSICS v0.89.0: 2D rigid bodies: circles, boxes, polygons, segments; fast balls that never pass through\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n\nPinball, Breakout, Asteroids with real collisions, an artillery game's grenades: bodies in a plane of x and y (the ground\nplane, or the side plane with the engine's z as y), stepped in a fixed order, so the same inputs give the same world.\n- const world = new E.Physics({ gravity: [0, 400] (left out: [0, 0]), substeps: 4, iterations: 8, sleep: true, on: { hit(a, b, info),\n  enter(sensor, body), exit(sensor, body), catch(kicker, body) } }). world.step(dt) in each fixed step (it splits dt in\n  substeps: none longer than dt / substeps). gravity is a vector (a pinball table's tilt: [0, 400] down its slope).\n- Bodies: world.circle(x, y, r, o), world.box(x, y, w, h, o), world.poly(x, y, points, o) (convex, points round x, y)\n  are dynamic by default; world.segment(a, b, o), world.chain(points, o) (a polyline; closed: true), world.arc(x, y, r,\n  a0, a1, o) (a curved rail as a chain) are static; world.add({ shape: 'circle' | 'box' | 'poly' | 'segment' | 'field',\n  type: 'dynamic' | 'kinematic' | 'static', ... }) any. A segment or polygon may have r: rounded by that much (a capsule).\n  o: { type, mass (else density * area; density .01), bounce (0..1, .3), friction (.4), damping (per second), angle,\n  vx, vy, spin (radians a second), layer (bits, 1), mask (bits it collides with, 0xffff), sensor (overlaps reported,\n  no push), bullet (a fast circle: swept, so it stops at what it would pass through), kick (a bumper's or slingshot's:\n  what it hits leaves at this speed at least, pixels a second, along the hit's normal), gravity (its scale, 1), maxSpeed, fixedRotation, data (yours) }.\n- A body: x, y, angle, vx, vy, spin, sleeping, off (true: it takes no part), held (caught by a kicker); b.impulse(ix, iy,\n  px, py), b.wake(), b.moveTo(x, y, angle, speed, turn) (a kinematic body goes there at that speed: paddles, doors).\n  Kinematic bodies are moved by code and give their speed to what they hit (flippers, paddles); static ones never move.\n- Helpers: world.flipper(x, y, { side: 'left' | 'right', len: 34, r0: 5, r1: 3, rest: .45, up: -.45, speed: 30 })\n  (a kinematic tapered bar; flip(true) swings it up, flip(false) back; y down the screen), world.bumper(x, y, r,\n  { kick: 260 }), world.slingshot(a, b, { kick: 220 }), world.kicker(x, y, { r: 6, hold: .6, dir: [0, -1], power: 700 })\n  (a sensor that catches a ball, holds it, then fires it: a saucer, a kickback; armed: false lets balls by).\n- Layers: a ball on a ramp ignores the table's walls: ball.mask = RAMP while it rides, a sensor at each end switching it.\n  A field: { shape: 'field', type: 'static', test(x, y, r) -> [nx, ny, depth] | null } collides with circles (the\n  terrain module's terrain.collider()).\n- world.ray(a, b, mask) -> { body, x, y, t } | null (the nearest hit along a to b); world.query(x, y) -> bodies there;\n  world.remove(b); world.wake(); world.bodies (in the order added); world.contacts (the last substep's: { a, b, nx, ny,\n  pts }); world.hash() (a proof's number); world.draw(g, to,\n  color) outlines every body (to(x, y) -> [sx, sy]: your plane on the screen).\n\n```js physics\nconst E = My3D2dge, world = new E.Physics({ gravity: [0, 600] });\nworld.chain([[0, 0], [0, 200], [160, 200], [160, 0]]);                    // a box open at the top\nconst L = world.flipper(40, 170, { side: 'left' }), ball = world.circle(64, 150, 5, { bullet: true, bounce: .4 });\nfor (let i = 0; i < 300 && !world.contacts.some(c => c.a === L || c.b === L); i++) world.step(1 / 120);   // it lands on it\nL.flip(true); for (let i = 0; i < 12; i++) world.step(1 / 120);\nif (!(ball.vy < -100)) throw new Error('the flipper fires it up');\nconst shot = world.circle(80, 100, 4, { bullet: true, vx: 9000 }); for (let i = 0; i < 30; i++) world.step(1 / 120);\nif (shot.x > 160) throw new Error('never through the wall');\n```\nRules: step it from the game's fixed step only (the same steps give the same world); a fast ball is a bullet; keep\npolygons convex (a concave shape is several bodies or a chain); give a table's walls a little thickness (r: 1) where\nballs press hard; draw your own art at the bodies' places (draw() is for checking).\n*/\n9233:      if (this.name) { const nw = E.font.width(this.name) + 12, nx = d.x + (this.portrait ? d.tx - 6 : 4); ui.box(g, nx, d.y - 12, nw, 14, { bg: this.bg, border: this.border }); E.font.text(g, th\n9235:      const mk = this._fx && this._fx[this.i], o = { outline: false, shadow: '#05040a' };\n9256:        this.choices.forEach((c, k) => { E.font.text(g, c, cx + 13, cy + 4 + k * d.lh, k === this.choice ? this.nameColor : this.color, { outline: false, shadow: '#05040a' }); if (k === this.choi\n9320:      const { labels, w, h, x, y, top: yy, rowH, k: K, first, vis } = this._layout(), T = { outline: false, shadow: '#05040a', scale: K };\n9322:      if (this.title) E.font.text(g, this.title, x + w / 2, y + 5 * K, this.pick, { align: 'center', outline: false, shadow: '#05040a', scale: K });\n648:     *  headless game draws: o.draw); ctx: its 2D context (r.ctx is the same) */\n649:    this.buf = canvas || (o && o.draw) ? mkCanvas(8, 8) : null; this.ctx = this.buf ? ctx2d(this.buf) : null;\n696:    if (this.buf) { this.buf.width = this.W + 2; this.buf.height = this.H + 2; this.ctx = ctx2d(this.buf); this.ctx._c = null; }\n1551:      this._g.putImageData(this._img, 0, 0); r.ctx.drawImage(this._cv, 0, 0);\n1552:      if (lit) { this._g2.putImageData(this._img2, 0, 0); const c = r.ctx; c.save(); c.globalCompositeOperation = 'lighter'; c.drawImage(this._cv2, 0, 0); \n1564:    r.ctx.drawImage(this._cv, 0, 0);\n1723:  get ctx() { return this.game.screen.ctx; }\n5654:      r.ctx.drawImage(ch.cv, X, Y); if (gpu && ch.info) r._iG.drawImage(ch.info, X, Y);\n558:class View {\n608:  iso: new View('iso', 'Isometric', 45, 30, Math.SQRT2, 1),                 // Diablo, Bastion (2:1 pixel iso)\n609:  threequarter: new View('threequarter', 'Three-quarter', 0, 55, 1.5, 1.35), // Zelda, Stardew, Enter the Gungeon\n610:  topdown: new View('topdown', 'Top-down', 0, 80, 1.5, 1.3),                 // Hotline Miami, GTA 1\n611:  brawler: new View('brawler', 'Brawler', 0, 25, 1.5, 1),                    // Streets of Rage, Castle Crashers","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6a88ba50-da75-48c3-bde0-396ebfab72e9","uuid":"c1465697-946b-4160-bdb3-986c2bc9a1c0","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:16:25.268Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== rhythm\n/*!\nmy-3D2dge module RHYTHM v0.89.0: charts on a song's steps, judged on the music clock: combos, grades, holds, a highway\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine only. Needs: no other module.\n\nPaRappa's, Beatmania's, Dance Dance Revolution's and Space Channel 5's play: notes on a song's steps, hit in time.\n- const rh = new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes: ['left', 'down', 'up', 'right'] (the actions, one a lane),\n  windows: { perfect: 40, great: 80, good: 120 } (ms either side), life: .5, lead: 1.6 (seconds of notes shown\n  ahead), voice: { wave: 'square', vol: .2, dur: .09 } (the call notes' sound), on: { judge(j, note), fail(rh),\n  done(rh) } }).\n- chart: a string a lane, a character a step of the song: 'x' a note, 'h' a held note's head and '=' while it is\n  held, 'c' a call (PaRappa's teacher: it sounds and shows, the player answers after), '.' none; '|' and spaces are\n  ignored. Or { parts: { A: [lanes], B: [lanes] }, order: 'A A B A' } (the parts one after another), or { track: 1,\n  lanes: 4 } (that track's notes, a lane by pitch, a note held three steps or more a hold).\n- rh.start() plays the song from its start, synced (it pauses with the game); rh.update() each step after the input:\n  a lane's press is judged by its distance in ms from its nearest note's time on the music clock (game.audio.pos:\n  game time, never the sound's own), a hold let go before its end drops, a note past the good window is missed, a\n  call sounds on its step (game.audio.sfx(voice, { step })).\n- rh.hit(lane), rh.release(lane): play a lane without its action (a bot, a lane of your own on a touch screen).\n- State: score, combo, maxCombo, counts { perfect, great, good, miss }, life (0..1, at 0 failed), accuracy (0..1),\n  grade ('S' 'A' 'B' 'C' 'D'), done, failed, last ({ j, lane, ms, t }: the last judgment, for its flash), notes\n  (each { lane, step, end, call, j, ms }), total (the notes to play).\n- rh.ahead() -> the notes to show: [{ note, dt (seconds to its time, < 0 past it), dtEnd }]; rh.draw(r, { x, y (the\n  target line's middle), dir: 'down' | 'up' | 'left' | 'right' (the way notes travel), len: 150 (pixels for lead\n  seconds), gap: 24 (between lanes), size: 8, colors, arrows: false (four lanes' notes as arrows: left, down, up,\n  right), call: false (draw the call notes instead) }) draws a highway on the overlay: the lanes, their targets, notes\n  and holds, each lane's flash.\n\n```js rhythm\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true }); game.start({ update() {}, draw() {} });\nconst song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, loop: false, len: 32, tracks: [{ wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h .' }] };\nconst rh = new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart: ['x...x...', '..x.....', '......h===', '.'] });\nrh.start(); const hits = [[0, 0], [2, 1], [4, 0], [6, 2]];\nfor (let i = 0; i < 400 && !rh.done; i++) {\n  game.advance(1 / 120); const s = game.audio.pos.step;\n  for (const h of hits) if (!h.done && s >= h[0]) { rh.hit(h[1]); h.done = true; }\n  if (s >= 9) rh.release(2); rh.update();\n}\nif (rh.counts.perfect !== 4 || rh.combo !== 4 || rh.grade !== 'S') throw new Error(JSON.stringify(rh.counts));\n```\nRules: judge on the music clock (rh does), never on the sound's; give the player the audio offset (Settings, Sound:\nits calibration) and keep the windows generous on a phone; draw notes from rh.ahead() each frame.\n*/\n=== mode7\n/*!\nmy-3D2dge module MODE7 v0.89.0: a perspective floor drawn a row at a time, a sky that turns with it, everything on it scaled by its distance\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n\nSuper Mario Kart's, F-Zero's and Pilotwings' view (the SNES's Mode 7): a camera at a height over a flat floor, looking\nalong a heading, pitched down; the floor drawn a screen row at a time, the sky above the horizon, and on the floor\nbillboards (rigs drawn at the size their distance gives, sprites, your own drawing) far to near.\n- const m7 = new E.Mode7({ floor: a TileMap (its floorTex) | (x, y) => [r, g, b] | a canvas (a texel a unit), size:\n  [w, h] (the floor in world units, for a function), outside: '#24402a' (beyond the floor) | wrap: true (it repeats),\n  sky: a Backdrop (full engine) | ['#top', '#bottom'], fog: { color, near, far } (far: nothing past it), far: 2400 }).\n- m7.cam = { x, y, h: 40 (height), angle: 0 (the heading, as E.angleTo gives it: 0 east, PI / 2 south; keep it\n  unwrapped, the sky turns with it), pitch: 12 (degrees down), fov: 70 (degrees across the height) };\n  m7.chase(body, { back: 56, h: 34, angle }) puts it behind a body (body.angle, or angle) each step.\n- In draw: m7.rig(rig, x, y, z), m7.sprite(spr or E.anim, x, y, z, { scale, flip, t }), m7.shape(id, x, y, z, { facing,\n  size, params, mats }) (full engine), m7.add(x, y, z, (g, sx, sy, k) => ...) gather billboards (k: screen pixels per world\n  unit there); m7.draw(r, cam) draws sky, floor, fog and them, far to near, as an overlay (in a split screen, in\n  r.viewport: give each player's cam). A billboard is flat, at its foot's scale: hit-test the box it was drawn in (from\n  m7.project and its size), not the world's view of it.\n- m7.project(x, y, z) -> [sx, sy, k] on the screen, or null behind the camera; m7.toFloor(sx, sy) -> [x, y], or null\n  above the horizon (both for the camera last drawn: HUD markers, a tap on the track). m7.horizon: its screen row.\n- Your own pass: m7.begin({ W, H, x, y, cx, cy, focal }, cam), then project, rowDepth(sy), drawFloor(g, rect),\n  view(k) (the engine view a rig is drawn with at k).\n- Resolution: the game's own pixels by default, as the SNES drew; m7.fullRes(game, true) each step draws at the\n  screen's own (sharper, slower; it returns the pixel size the game had), false gives the game's pixels back.\n\n```js mode7\nconst E = My3D2dge, m7 = new E.Mode7({ floor: (x, y) => ((x >> 4) + (y >> 4)) & 1 ? [80, 160, 80] : [60, 130, 60], size: [512, 512] });\nm7.cam = { x: 256, y: 400, h: 40, angle: -Math.PI / 2, pitch: 12, fov: 70 };\nm7.begin({ W: 320, H: 240 });\nconst p = m7.project(256, 300, 0), q = m7.toFloor(p[0], p[1]);\nif (Math.abs(q[0] - 256) > .01 || Math.abs(q[1] - 300) > .01 || p[1] <= m7.horizon) throw new Error('a floor point and back');\n```\nRules: m7.draw covers its viewport (draw nothing under it you need to see); move the camera in update, not draw; a\nbody's angle and the camera's heading are the same angle; billboards are gathered again every frame.\n*/\n=== road\n/*!\nmy-3D2dge module ROAD v0.89.0: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n\nOutRun's, Pole Position's, Hang-On's and Road Rash's view: the road a run of short segments, each a band of grass, rumble\nand road drawn smaller with its distance, bending and rising, and what stands beside it scaled the same way.\n- const road = new E.Road({ segment: 200 (a segment's length, world units), width: 2000 (half the road), lanes: 3,\n  rumble: 3 (segments a stripe), draw: 240 (segments ahead), fov: 100, height: 1000 (the camera over the road), colors:\n  { road: [a, b], grass: [a, b], rumble: [a, b], lane, wall: [a, b], roof, portal }, fog: { color, density: 5 } | null, sky:\n  a Backdrop (full engine) | '#color', square: true (one focal length: a unit across is a unit up on a screen of any\n  shape; without it the picture stretches to the screen's, as the arcades' did) }).\n- Build it: road.add(n, { curve: -6..6 (+ bends right), hill: units up (- down) over the n segments, tunnel: true,\n  colors }) (curves eased in and out); road.place(z, offset, what, scale): scenery at distance z, offset across (-1\n  and 1: the road's edges; beyond: roadside); what: an E.sprite or E.anim (scale: world units a pixel, 8) or {\n  draw(g, sx, sy, scale), w: its width in units }. road.length: the lap (it loops).\n- Each frame: road.draw(r, { z (the camera's distance along), x (across, in half roads), h (its height over the road),\n  turn (the sky's offset: add curve * speed each step), cars: [{ z, x, w, draw(g, sx, sy, scale) }] }) as an overlay\n  over the frame (in a split screen, in r.viewport). A hill's crest hides what lies past it. The player's car, drawn\n  at the screen's bottom, is road.ahead(h) past z.\n- For the game: road.curveAt(z) (how hard it bends there: the push outward), road.yAt(z) (its height), road.hits(z, x,\n  w) (the scenery a body w half roads wide touches there), road.project(z, x, y) -> [sx, sy, scale] for the camera\n  last drawn (scale * a width in units = pixels).\n\n```js road\nconst E = My3D2dge, road = new E.Road({ segment: 200 });\nroad.add(50); road.add(60, { curve: 4, hill: 1200 }); road.add(40, { curve: -3, hill: -1200 }); road.place(3000, -1.4, { w: 300, draw() {} });\nif (road.length !== 150 * 200 || road.curveAt(80 * 200) <= 0 || !(road.yAt(110 * 200) > 0) || road.hits(3000, -1.3, .1).length !== 1) throw new Error('a road');\n```\nRules: z grows ahead and wraps at road.length; x is in half roads (0 the middle line); build the road before the first\ndraw; cars and scenery are drawn far to near after the road under them.\n*/\n=== physics\n/*!\nmy-3D2dge module PHYSICS v0.89.0: 2D rigid bodies: circles, boxes, polygons, segments; fast balls that never pass through\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n\nPinball, Breakout, Asteroids with real collisions, an artillery game's grenades: bodies in a plane of x and y (the ground\nplane, or the side plane with the engine's z as y), stepped in a fixed order, so the same inputs give the same world.\n- const world = new E.Physics({ gravity: [0, 400] (left out: [0, 0]), substeps: 4, iterations: 8, sleep: true, on: { hit(a, b, info),\n  enter(sensor, body), exit(sensor, body), catch(kicker, body) } }). world.step(dt) in each fixed step (it splits dt in\n  substeps: none longer than dt / substeps). gravity is a vector (a pinball table's tilt: [0, 400] down its slope).\n- Bodies: world.circle(x, y, r, o), world.box(x, y, w, h, o), world.poly(x, y, points, o) (convex, points round x, y)\n  are dynamic by default; world.segment(a, b, o), world.chain(points, o) (a polyline; closed: true), world.arc(x, y, r,\n  a0, a1, o) (a curved rail as a chain) are static; world.add({ shape: 'circle' | 'box' | 'poly' | 'segment' | 'field',\n  type: 'dynamic' | 'kinematic' | 'static', ... }) any. A segment or polygon may have r: rounded by that much (a capsule).\n  o: { type, mass (else density * area; density .01), bounce (0..1, .3), friction (.4), damping (per second), angle,\n  vx, vy, spin (radians a second), layer (bits, 1), mask (bits it collides with, 0xffff), sensor (overlaps reported,\n  no push), bullet (a fast circle: swept, so it stops at what it would pass through), kick (a bumper's or slingshot's:\n  what it hits leaves at this speed at least, pixels a second, along the hit's normal), gravity (its scale, 1), maxSpeed, fixedRotation, data (yours) }.\n- A body: x, y, angle, vx, vy, spin, sleeping, off (true: it takes no part), held (caught by a kicker); b.impulse(ix, iy,\n  px, py), b.wake(), b.moveTo(x, y, angle, speed, turn) (a kinematic body goes there at that speed: paddles, doors).\n  Kinematic bodies are moved by code and give their speed to what they hit (flippers, paddles); static ones never move.\n- Helpers: world.flipper(x, y, { side: 'left' | 'right', len: 34, r0: 5, r1: 3, rest: .45, up: -.45, speed: 30 })\n  (a kinematic tapered bar; flip(true) swings it up, flip(false) back; y down the screen), world.bumper(x, y, r,\n  { kick: 260 }), world.slingshot(a, b, { kick: 220 }), world.kicker(x, y, { r: 6, hold: .6, dir: [0, -1], power: 700 })\n  (a sensor that catches a ball, holds it, then fires it: a saucer, a kickback; armed: false lets balls by).\n- Layers: a ball on a ramp ignores the table's walls: ball.mask = RAMP while it rides, a sensor at each end switching it.\n  A field: { shape: 'field', type: 'static', test(x, y, r) -> [nx, ny, depth] | null } collides with circles (the\n  terrain module's terrain.collider()).\n- world.ray(a, b, mask) -> { body, x, y, t } | null (the nearest hit along a to b); world.query(x, y) -> bodies there;\n  world.remove(b); world.wake(); world.bodies (in the order added); world.contacts (the last substep's: { a, b, nx, ny,\n  pts }); world.hash() (a proof's number); world.draw(g, to,\n  color) outlines every body (to(x, y) -> [sx, sy]: your plane on the screen).\n\n```js physics\nconst E = My3D2dge, world = new E.Physics({ gravity: [0, 600] });\nworld.chain([[0, 0], [0, 200], [160, 200], [160, 0]]);                    // a box open at the top\nconst L = world.flipper(40, 170, { side: 'left' }), ball = world.circle(64, 150, 5, { bullet: true, bounce: .4 });\nfor (let i = 0; i < 300 && !world.contacts.some(c => c.a === L || c.b === L); i++) world.step(1 / 120);   // it lands on it\nL.flip(true); for (let i = 0; i < 12; i++) world.step(1 / 120);\nif (!(ball.vy < -100)) throw new Error('the flipper fires it up');\nconst shot = world.circle(80, 100, 4, { bullet: true, vx: 9000 }); for (let i = 0; i < 30; i++) world.step(1 / 120);\nif (shot.x > 160) throw new Error('never through the wall');\n```\nRules: step it from the game's fixed step only (the same steps give the same world); a fast ball is a bullet; keep\npolygons convex (a concave shape is several bodies or a chain); give a table's walls a little thickness (r: 1) where\nballs press hard; draw your own art at the bodies' places (draw() is for checking).\n*/\n9233:      if (this.name) { const nw = E.font.width(this.name) + 12, nx = d.x + (this.portrait ? d.tx - 6 : 4); ui.box(g, nx, d.y - 12, nw, 14, { bg: this.bg, border: this.border }); E.font.text(g, th\n9235:      const mk = this._fx && this._fx[this.i], o = { outline: false, shadow: '#05040a' };\n9256:        this.choices.forEach((c, k) => { E.font.text(g, c, cx + 13, cy + 4 + k * d.lh, k === this.choice ? this.nameColor : this.color, { outline: false, shadow: '#05040a' }); if (k === this.choi\n9320:      const { labels, w, h, x, y, top: yy, rowH, k: K, first, vis } = this._layout(), T = { outline: false, shadow: '#05040a', scale: K };\n9322:      if (this.title) E.font.text(g, this.title, x + w / 2, y + 5 * K, this.pick, { align: 'center', outline: false, shadow: '#05040a', scale: K });\n648:     *  headless game draws: o.draw); ctx: its 2D context (r.ctx is the same) */\n649:    this.buf = canvas || (o && o.draw) ? mkCanvas(8, 8) : null; this.ctx = this.buf ? ctx2d(this.buf) : null;\n696:    if (this.buf) { this.buf.width = this.W + 2; this.buf.height = this.H + 2; this.ctx = ctx2d(this.buf); this.ctx._c = null; }\n1551:      this._g.putImageData(this._img, 0, 0); r.ctx.drawImage(this._cv, 0, 0);\n1552:      if (lit) { this._g2.putImageData(this._img2, 0, 0); const c = r.ctx; c.save(); c.globalCompositeOperation = 'lighter'; c.drawImage(this._cv2, 0, 0); \n1564:    r.ctx.drawImage(this._cv, 0, 0);\n1723:  get ctx() { return this.game.screen.ctx; }\n5654:      r.ctx.drawImage(ch.cv, X, Y); if (gpu && ch.info) r._iG.drawImage(ch.info, X, Y);\n558:class View {\n608:  iso: new View('iso', 'Isometric', 45, 30, Math.SQRT2, 1),                 // Diablo, Bastion (2:1 pixel iso)\n609:  threequarter: new View('threequarter', 'Three-quarter', 0, 55, 1.5, 1.35), // Zelda, Stardew, Enter the Gungeon\n610:  topdown: new View('topdown', 'Top-down', 0, 80, 1.5, 1.3),                 // Hotline Miami, GTA 1\n611:  brawler: new View('brawler', 'Brawler', 0, 25, 1.5, 1),                    // Streets of Rage, Castle Crashers","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Nf2Sss6pMmAqxMjTuezipk","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
