{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F2Jahbh3XKWeNeGAvhUEhk","type":"tool_result","content":"762:    this.held = new Set(); this.clock = 0; this._pt = {}; this._used = {};\n12833:    this.world = world; this.id = world._id++; this.sleeping = false; this.held = null; this.to = this.to || null;\n1309:Input.DEFAULT = {\n6305:const PT_DEFAULT = { kind: 'solid', style: 'block', side: '#8a7a9a' };\n4881:Humanoid.hat = (id, draw) => { HUMANOID_HATS[id] = draw; return draw; };\n  start() { this.reset(); this.game.audio.music(this.song, { sync: true, restart: true, loop: false }); this.started = true; }\n  // seconds a step lasts now, and the music's step now (the music clock: game time)\n  _spb() { const p = this.game.audio.pos; return 60 / (p.bpm || this.song.bpm || 120) / (this.song.steps || 4); }\n  /** a press in a lane: judged against the nearest note there within the good window (a hold starts held) */\n  hit(lane) {\n    if (!this.started || this.done) return null;\n    this.down[lane] = true;\n    const s = this.game.audio.pos.step, spb = this._spb(); let best = null, bd = 1e9;\n    for (const n of this.notes) { if (n.lane !== lane || n.call || n.j) continue; const d = Math.abs(s - n.step) * spb * 1000; if (d <= this.windows.good && d < bd) { best = n; bd = d; } if (n.step > s + 4 * this.song.steps) break; }\n    if (!best) return null;\n    const ms = Math.round((s - best.step) * spb * 1000), w = this.windows, a = Math.abs(ms);\n    this._judge(best, a <= w.perfect ? 'perfect' : a <= w.great ? 'great' : 'good', ms);\n    if (best.end > best.step) best.holding = true;\n    return best;\n  update() {\n    if (!this.started || this.done) return;\n    const I = this.game.input, A = this.game.audio, s = A.pos.step, spb = this._spb();\n    this.lanes.forEach((a, i) => { if (I.pressed(a)) this.hit(i); else if (this.down[i] && I.released(a)) this.release(i); });\n    for (const n of this.notes) {\n      if (n.step > s + 8 * this.song.steps) break;\n      if (n.call) { if (!n.played && (n.step - s) * spb < .1) { n.played = true; A.sfx(Object.assign({ freq: CALL[n.lane % CALL.length] }, this.voice), { step: n.step }); } if (!n.j && s >= n.step) { n.j = 'call'; this._flash[n.lane] = this\n      if (!n.j && (s - n.step) * spb * 1000 > this.windows.good) this._judge(n, 'miss', 0);\n      if (n.holding && s >= n.end) { n.holding = false; this.score += 100; }\n      if (this.done) return;\n    }\n    const p = A.pos; if (!p.playing && p.t > 0) { this.done = true; if (this.on.done) this.on.done(this); }\n  }\n## 21c. Props\n\n- `E.PROPS: torch, candle, candelabra, chandelier, brazier, window, banner, pillar, statue, crate, barrel, chest, pot, sign, fence, lamp, door, tree, pine, bush, flowers, grass, rock, crystal, bones, skull, vines, cobweb, lantern, streetlamp, awning, hydrant, \n- `E.prop(name, o = {})`: build (and cache) a prop: { frames: [sprite], glow: [sprite] | null, w, h }\n\n## 21e. Shapes\n\n- `E.SHAPES: barrel, crate, chest, table, chair, stool, bench, bed, bookcase, shelf, pot, jar, sack, cart, ... (25)`: the shapes by id: { about, tags, mats: { slot: material }, parts | make(params), params, foot, lights, flames } (the core library's, the sets'\n- `E.addAssets(set)`: register a store set (src/assets/sets/*.js: { set, format: 1, credit, sources, materials, shapes, sprites }): its entries are named 'SET:id' (so one set never changes another's, or the core's) and find their own set's materials and shapes\n- `E.materialTile(id, o = {})`: a material's pattern as a tile of pixels, for a 3D renderer's texture: E.materialTile(id, { size: 32 (world units square: it repeats every size; a face pattern's whole face), px: 2 (pixels a unit), lid: false (true: as on a face\n- `E.shapeBox(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: where a placed shape stands, as both engines collide with it: E.shapeBox(id | entry, x, y, z, { facing, scale, flip, params }) -> { x, y (its footprint's middle), z, top, hx, hy (half its footprint, along its own x and \n- `E.shapeInfo(id, o = {})`: what a shape draws, for tools and tests: E.shapeInfo(id, { view: 'iso', facing, scale, mats, params }) -> { w, h, ox, oy, tris, prims (its primitives), parts (each primitive's pixels on screen: 0 is never seen there), colors (disti\n- `E.shapeMesh(id, o = {})`: a shape's triangles, for a 3D renderer (the 3D engine's world.shape): E.shapeMesh(id | entry, { params, mats, seg }) -> { groups: [{ mat, key, lid, curved, face, pos, nrm, uv }], bounds [x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1] } in the entry's own\n- `E.shapeMesh({ seg })`: seg(r): the segments round a radius r (default 8 to 24)\n- `E.shapeMesh() → groups`: each one's mat (the material ready to draw: E.material's), key (its id), lid (true: the faces looking up or down, which some patterns draw their own way), curved (turned or round faces: planks run up them), face (a pattern drawn onc\n- `E.shapeSprite(id, o = {})`: a shape as a sprite (E.sprite's kind: r.sprite, px.sprite, inventories, HUDs, portraits): E.shapeSprite(id, { view: 'iso', facing, size (its scale, 1), mats, params, outline: true | a color | false }). The view is a name or a Vie\n\n-- plant pot\nkaykit-furniture-bits:cactus-medium-a shape     283 tok  leafy green succulent in a round terracotta pot  [pla\nkaykit-furniture-bits:cactus-medium-b shape     455 tok  bushy green succulent in a terracotta pot  [plant dec\nkaykit-furniture-bits:cactus-small-b shape     298 tok  small green succulent in a little terracotta pot  [pla\nkenney-nature:pot-small            shape      86 tok  small round wooden plant pot, flared rim  [container gar\nkenney-nature:pot-large            shape      78 tok  wide low wooden planter tub  [container garden farm]\n-- bench\nbench                              shape      57 tok  plank bench on two trestles  [furniture tavern]\nkaykit-halloween-bits:bench        shape     204 tok  low weathered grey-brown wooden bench on slab legs  [fur\nkenney-fantasy-town:stall-bench    shape    