rch; the plan's recipes were followed.\",\n    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\",\n    \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n    \"usage\": \"added on import\"\n  },\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"About 14. Laundry Line too hard for the average bot, its passive run outlasting the test guard, Tray Service over too quickly, the Rail's three stars out of reach, the hub round sending no ghost data, a mouse and keyboard source race, and a dark pause menu from a theme that never applied, plus several layout overlaps found in screenshots. Nobody played it by hand, so feel on a real controller is untested.\",\n    \"1. The hub round sent nothing during the harness's auto run, which would have kept the game out of AI Hub sessions.\",\n    \"The bot sweep over every activity and tier against the star targets. It found every balance problem in one table and made tuning a matter of minutes.\",\n    \"The determinism checks. They passed the first time and never failed; the engine's fixed step already guarantees them.\"\n  ],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"Real motion capture playing on pixel-art rigs, and the headless game.advance. A whole five-day playthrough runs in seconds with real taps, drawn on a stand-in.\",\n    \"Yes. I guessed that the Shell was not yet made when my theme call ran, and a guard silently skipped the theme until a screenshot showed the dark menu. I also guessed a Backdrop sea layer would stay at the horizon; it filled the sky.\",\n    \"The Lean: the balance model, the shared intent object that devices and bots both fill, and the Plate. Also the session flow that lets one scene serve story, Class, attract and the hub round.\",\n    \"Layering my own wobble and hand poses over mocap, where each clip turns the rig by its own heading. The plan's recipes solved it; without them it would have taken a long time. Telling keyboard from mouse also needs game-side work.\",\n    \"One patch: E.Dialog's three hard-coded near-black text shadows now read this.shadow, because they smeared on a white dialog box. Nothing else.\",\n    \"Let input.lastDevice report mouse movement, so games do not need their own comparison to decide which device a prompt should show.\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"The balance of freedom and a tested plan: every recipe marked as tested worked, so effort went into the game and not into the engine's traps.\",\n    \"The plan names engine v0.88.0 and the fetched handoff is v0.89.0, so the Dialog patch's line numbers differed slightly. 'Done' also has to be judged without a person playing it.\",\n    \"Judging feel with nobody to play it. Bots can prove a balance band, but not whether a lean feels good on a real stick.\",\n    \"Add a short note on how to report what could not be felt or heard here, since the brief asks for a complete, polished game that no one on this computer can actually hold.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Why Fit\",\n    \"tagline\": \"A five-day stay. You know why.\",\n    \"description\": \"A gentle, deadpan comedy about a five-day stay at a wellness retreat, where one skill, your balance, drives twelve short activities. A needy talking scale and two serene wooden instructors see you through.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Sports\",\n    \"source\": \"Wii Fit\",\n    \"series\": \"\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Lean with the left stick, WASD or the mouse; breathe and exert with R2, Space or left click; confirm with Cross, Enter or a click.\",\n    \"tags\": [\"pixel art\", \"comedy\", \"versus\", \"arcade\", \"story\", \"2d\"]\n  }\n}\nEOF\npython3 -c \"import json;json.load(open('../exit-interview.json'));print('json ok')\"\nnode build.mjs; python3 tests/shot.py tests/shots \"about=|G.game.go(\\\"about\\\",undefined,{fade:0})\" \"pause=#act/stork/0|G.game.pause()\" \"stepb=#act/step/0|(()=>{const s=G.game.scene;s.phase=\\\"play\\\";s.t=0;const c=s.ctx.local;c.bot=\\\"expert