{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjLfgjhPZtavQiW8SFWX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The final build passes the full test command in one run: **941 passed, 0 failed, exit 0**. Everything on this computer that the stop hook raised is now checked, and this pass also found and fixed two real bugs. The one item left, a person playing the game, can't be done here.\n\n**What the stop hook raised:**\n- **Dialog shadow patch:** now checked on a rendered dialog. There are no dark shadow pixels in the text area with the patch on, and they come back with it off. The dark edges left on the box and name tab are the engine's normal drop shadows.\n- **Attract on touch-only devices:** now checked on three profiles: phone (Pixel 7), tablet (iPad Pro 11) and iPhone on WebKit. All three start attract behind the \"Controller or keyboard required\" notice. The tablet run confirms it waits about 10 game seconds, and the phone run confirms a tap doesn't stop it.\n- **M1 \"stop and tune here\":** I added the part a script can measure. Scripted players now play all 12 activities through the real keyboard and mouse code, and each earns at least one star on both devices. In Stork, keys score within 0.15 of the stick model, which is the plan's claim.\n\n**Bugs this found, both fixed:**\n- **Holding Space blocked the mouse:** holding Space to walk stopped the mouse from leaning, so Laundry Line was close to unplayable that way.\n- **Hoop Hips on keys:** tapping W D S A at the right rhythm still scored about half what the mouse did (0.44 against 0.96), because each tap made the spin reading jump out of the \"just right\" band. Keys now stay within 0.25 of the mouse score.\n\nA smaller fix: the title's prompt chip no longer sits on top of Tare's dialog.\n\n**Still not done:** nobody has played the game or listened to it. Scripted players show each activity can be scored on keyboard and mouse, but not that it feels good. Real controller feel, how the audio sounds and the view on a real TV are all unconfirmed. TASK.md says these are checked as far as possible here and \"never required\", so I consider the goal met, but they are the first things to check.\n\nThe Source Information and feedback in my earlier message still stand, with two updates that are also on the About screen and in `exit-interview.json`. Testing Feedback now counts about 16 issues and names the two bugs above, and the Testing field mentions the scripted device players.\n\nEverything is in `work/`, and nothing is committed to git:\n- `WhyFit-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-221447.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n- `PROGRESS.md`\n- `WhyFit-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-221447/` (dev files)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1377,"cache_read_input_tokens":470601,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1377},"output_tokens":698,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6a88ba50-da75-48c3-bde0-396ebfab72e9","uuid":"5f34f428-6042-4a71-8ab0-8f8a2c31e361","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:52:54.548Z","request_id":"req_011CgjLffvqsJABgpXqKm742"}
