{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjMaDAEyqfyqkjbjRub5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The final build passes the full test command in one run: **944 passed, 0 failed, exit 0**. Both files TASK.md asks for are in the folder, and `exit-interview.json` parses.\n\n**The stop hook's objection:** it wants a person to have played the game, listened to it and seen it on a TV. I can't do that here, and I won't claim it happened. The goal covers what \"can be done on this computer\", and TASK.md's section \"What this computer doesn't have\" lists no physical controller, nobody to listen and no TV. It says to \"test with the stand-ins\" and that the real thing is \"never required\". I've done each stand-in it names:\n\n| TASK.md says | Done |\n|---|---|\n| Emulate a controller with a stubbed standard pad | Stick, trigger, ✕, ✕ and A prompts, and a whole Stork Stand on the stub stick, which earns a star |\n| Check sound by what Web Audio produces | Music, voice and effects buses are non-silent; `OfflineAudioContext` renders the gibberish voice; the Eyes Closed tone sounds |\n| Judge the 10-foot view from 1920×1080 screenshots | Looked at title, Card, Plate, results, island and the activities, and re-shot the screens I changed |\n| Play multiplayer with two pages | Hub harness passes at 1 to 4 players, and I saw ghosts in a two-player round |\n| Use phone and tablet profiles for touch | Notice, Settings button and attract checked on three profiles |\n\n**This last pass found more that mattered:**\n- **M4's bar was never measured:** the beat click is now confirmed louder than the music at the default 10%.\n- **Coastal Jog:** my own earlier sky change had turned the horizon into towering teal cliffs. Fixed.\n- **Class:** Player 1 was off the left edge of the screen. Fixed.\n- **Hoop Hips:** the \"Just right\" label overlapped its dial. Fixed.\n\nNo test caught any of those three; they only showed up when I looked at the screenshots. Other visual problems could remain on screens I didn't re-shoot after later changes.\n\n**For whoever plays it first:** real stick feel, how the music and voices sound, and the view on a real TV are all still unconfirmed.\n\nThe Source Information and feedback from my earlier message still stand. The exit interview and About screen now count about 19 issues caught, including the Jog and Class bugs.\n\nEverything is in `work/`, and nothing is committed to git:\n- `WhyFit-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-221447.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n- `PROGRESS.md`\n- `WhyFit-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-221447/` (dev files)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":932,"cache_read_input_tokens":483270,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":932},"output_tokens":726,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6a88ba50-da75-48c3-bde0-396ebfab72e9","uuid":"137206f7-f574-4e58-9886-dd279e4d4861","timestamp":"2026-11-05T07:04:46.586Z","request_id":"req_011CgjMaBrs7fgUgpf9gk2fU"}
