{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjNVjohUSiwTBRN1yMgL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Why Fit** is finished: every check I can run on this computer is done, and the only thing missing is a person playing it. The final build passes the full test command in one run, **944 passed, 0 failed, exit 0**. Both files TASK.md asks for are in the folder, and `exit-interview.json` parses. The two leftover servers belong to other agents' folders, so I left them alone, and none of my own processes are still running.\n\n**What this last pass changed:** I had said some screens might not have been re-checked, so I went through them at 1920×1080, including several I'd never looked at. It found five more problems that no test had caught, all now fixed:\n- The player's character was missing from Tare's Day.\n- A street lamp stood right where the player spawns on the island at dusk, with a harsh green glow.\n- The Pose Viewer's rig was almost entirely hidden.\n- Class names were hard to read, and a prompt chip covered the Step highway.\n- The Rail heading and the festival's \"Next\" line had low contrast.\n\nI re-shot those screens after the fixes. The jog, hoop, Class menu and podium were checked in the round before and haven't changed since. The final rebuild changed only the exit interview's text, which the About screen shows.\n\n**What I'm not claiming:** nobody has played this game or heard it, and I can't change that. That includes the plan's M1 \"stop and tune here\" step, which I took as far as scripted players on real keyboard and mouse code, plus a stubbed stick. TASK.md lists no physical controller, nobody to listen and no TV among the things this computer lacks, and says to \"test with the stand-ins\". So the stop hook's remaining objection asks for something outside \"can be done on this computer\", and more rounds here won't resolve it.\n\n**What to check first when someone plays it:** how the lean feels on a real stick, how the music and voices sound, and how it reads on a real TV. Tuning numbers came from bots, so expect some adjusting; the Dev Mode sliders in the pause menu are there for that.\n\nThe Source Information and feedback from my earlier message still stand, with these updates:\n- Testing Feedback now counts about 24 issues.\n- The least-helpful-test answer now also notes that looking at every screen found bugs the passing checks missed.\n- The Testing field also mentions the scripted device players.\n\nThe About screen and `exit-interview.json` have the current wording.\n\nEverything is in `work/`, and nothing is committed to git:\n- `WhyFit-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-221447.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n- `PROGRESS.md`\n- `WhyFit-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-221447/` (dev files)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":535,"cache_read_input_tokens":500600,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":535},"output_tokens":652,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6a88ba50-da75-48c3-bde0-396ebfab72e9","uuid":"11e0c1b5-76bf-4350-94a5-0d61669e46d0","timestamp":"2026-11-05T07:16:51.772Z","request_id":"req_011CgjNVjRtWumV9mae8szeS"}
