{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjNWcRESWJ7NAx9oy8Xa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm stopping here: no further work on this computer can meet this objection. It asks for a person to play and hear the game, and that can't happen here. I won't report a human check that didn't happen, and more test rounds wouldn't change the answer.\n\n**Evidence on each side:**\n- **Stick, sound and TV view:** TASK.md says this computer has \"no physical controller\", \"nobody to listen\" and \"no TV\". It says to test with the stand-ins and that anything needing the real thing is \"never required\". I ran all three stand-ins: a stubbed pad, Web Audio level checks and 1920×1080 screenshots.\n- **M1 \"stop and tune here\":** this is the one place the plan's wording goes further than a script can, since it says \"feels good\". The balance bands hold, and scripted players earn at least one star on all 12 activities through the real keyboard and mouse code. Whether it feels good is still unknown, and I've said so in every report and in the exit interview.\n- **Deliverables:** the game and `exit-interview.json` are in `work/`, and the final build passes 944 of 944 checks.\n\n**Your call:** the hook reads those human-play items as still required, and I read them as outside \"can be done on this computer\".\n- **If you agree with me:** the work is complete, and `/goal clear` will end the loop.\n- **If you want them met:** someone needs to play the HTML file on a real controller and TV with sound on. I can then tune from their notes, using the Dev Mode sliders' values or what they report."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1170,"cache_read_input_tokens":501135,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1170},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","spe